From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: results Windows gives for Map, surface formats, command lists, WIC targets

Ground truth from Wine's d2d1 tests (todo_wine blocks recorded on Windows):
 - ID2D1Bitmap1::Map checks the access before the state: reading and writing need
   the CPU access of the texture (a bitmap made for reading only refuses writing),
   discarding needs a dynamic texture; mapping twice is WRONG_STATE only after the
   access was accepted.
 - A bitmap made from a DXGI surface (CreateBitmapFromDxgiSurface, CreateSharedBitmap
   of a surface) with a pixel format Direct2D cannot draw (straight alpha, unknown
   alpha) is D2DERR_UNSUPPORTED_PIXEL_FORMAT; render targets keep making their own
   target bitmap with whatever alpha mode they were asked for.
 - Closing a command list that is the target of a device context removes it as target.
 - GetSurface of the target of a WIC render target is E_FAIL (the surface is kept
   hidden), of other bitmaps without a surface D2DERR_INVALID_CALL.
 - A WIC render target holds the bitmap locked for writing from BeginDraw to
   EndDraw; a lock held by somebody else fails EndDraw with WINCODEC_ERR_ALREADYLOCKED.
 - GetDC of a DC render target with no DC bound is D2DERR_WRONG_STATE; BeginDraw
   on it no longer clears a target that does not exist (the test crashed there).
Removed the todo_wine marks that now pass (d2d1.c), among them the geometry area
and grayscale ones that earlier work had already fixed.
